The Drummer's grooves: the Groove MIDI Dataset
  https://magenta.tensorflow.org/datasets/groove
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  Copyright Google LLC. Groove MIDI Dataset v1.0.0, by Jon Gillick, Adam
  Roberts, Jesse Engel, Douglas Eck and David Bamman, recorded by Google's
  Magenta team with ten drummers.
  The license is at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  resources/drummer/grooves.json is made from the dataset's MIDI files by
  tools/build_grooves.py: the 4/4 performances of ten styles, their drum
  notes grouped into the Drummer's eleven pieces, cut into bars and fills,
  and scored for complexity and loudness. The notes' timing and velocities
  are the drummers' own. The dataset itself isn't part of Ikaros Studio.


Controller maps: Ardour's MIDI maps
  https://ardour.org (share/midi_maps in https://github.com/Ardour/ardour)
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
  Copyright the maps' authors, named in each map file.
  Most profiles in resources/controllers are made from Ardour's maps by
  tools/controllers/convert_ardour_maps.py (Ardour commit d34a51e): their
  transport and track buttons, and the knob numbers for the knob layouts.
  The port names, the knob layouts and the Arturia MiniLab 3 profile are our
  own. The maps themselves aren't part of Ikaros Studio.


Sounds
  Ikaros Basics, the sound pack that comes with the app, is made from scratch
  by tools/generate_sounds.py. It contains no third-party samples, and it's
  released under CC0 1.0 (public domain): use the sounds however you like.


Downloadable sound packs
  These aren't part of the app: they're downloaded from More Sounds. Each pack
  keeps its own LICENSE.txt with the original license and what was changed
  (only the samples its instruments play are kept, WAV samples are converted
  to FLAC, and some MIDI controllers are added for the Sound tab's knobs).
  They're built by tools/packs/build_packs.py.

